<title>USA: Mylan wins FDA approval on nausea treatment.</title>
<headline>Mylan wins FDA approval on nausea treatment.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mylan Laboratories Inc said Tuesday it received U.S. Food and Drug Administration approval to make and market a generic drug used to control severe nausea and vomiting.</p>
<p>The drug, Prochlorperazine Maleate, is also used to manage manifestations of psychotic disorders. It was approved in tablet form of 5 mg and 10 mg strengths.</p>
<p>The drug is the generic equivalent of Compazine, a SmithKline Beecham compound.</p>
</text>
